Revision history for Email-Barcode-Decode

0.05   not released yet
    - replaced Image::Magick with Imager; ImageMagick 6.9.11 (Debian 12)
      returned empty YUV blobs, which made Barcode::ZBar segfault
    - die with "raster size mismatch" instead of passing a short raster to
      Barcode::ZBar
    - enhancers simplified to plain grayscale and a black/white threshold;
      they now get an Imager object and return ($raw, 'Y800', $width, $height)
    - PDF pages are rendered with `pdftoppm -gray` (poppler-utils) instead of
      Ghostscript: lossless grayscale instead of JPEG, PDF-only parser
      instead of a PostScript interpreter; the long side of each page is
      rendered at $MAX_HEIGHT pixels (was 150 dpi), so a small PDF with
      huge pages cannot fill the disk
    - attached_files of PDF pages are now named <name>-pdf-page-N.pgm
      (was <name>-pdf-pageN.jpg); page numbers are zero-padded, which fixes
      the page order of PDFs with 10 or more pages
    - security: attachment filenames are reduced to their base name, and
      each attachment is saved in its own numbered sub-directory of the
      temporary directory; a filename such as ../../.bashrc could write
      outside of it, and attachments with equal filenames overwrote each
      other; control characters are removed and names are shortened to
      200 bytes, so such names no longer make new die
    - images with an alpha channel or 16 bits per sample no longer die with
      "raster size mismatch"; transparent areas are scanned as white
    - get_symbols skips attachments that Imager cannot read (text files,
      unsupported image formats, PDFs without pdftoppm) instead of dying
    - email_name and email_from no longer die (Email::Address was never
      loaded); they use Email::Address::XS now and return undef when there
      is no From header or the address is invalid (e.g. "From: <>"), without
      warnings
    - attachments inside nested multiparts are found
    - warn when pdftoppm fails, e.g. on a damaged PDF, with the exit status
      or the signal that killed it; the warning is transliterated to ASCII
      with Text::Unidecode
    - page limit of PDF attachments is configurable via $MAX_PDF_PAGES
    - each attachment is read once per get_symbols call instead of once per
      enhancer
    - File::Find::Rule is no longer needed
    - documentation extended: requirements, accessors, all public methods,
      configuration variables, enhancer contract, license

0.04   21 September 2016
    - fixes to still work after debian/jessie
      libmagickwand-6.q16-2 libmagickcore-6.q16-2 imagemagick-common packages
      security update to 8:6.8.9.9-5+deb8u4

0.03   18 March 2016
    - improved B/W enhancing of image to be decoded

0.02    4 Feb 2016
    - scaling down images to 1500px, bigger images may not work well with Barcode::ZBar::Image
    - normalize and sharpen contrast before decoding

0.01    4 Jan 2013
        First version, released on an unsuspecting world.

